item.text:
Accepted new evidence:

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DR Congo: Martial Law Brings Crackdown in East","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-03-22","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/03/22/dr-congo-martial-law-brings-crackdown-east","claim":"HRW says the military and police curtailed freedom of expression, used lethal force against peaceful demonstrations, and arbitrarily detained and prosecuted activists, journalists, and political opposition members in North Kivu and Ituri under martial law declared by Tshisekedi's administration.","locator":"lines 616-620","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous rights report with explicit attribution to Tshisekedi's administration and concrete examples of coercive repression.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period and the same emergency regime that continued through 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Tshisekedi's administration, which declared and maintained the martial law framework.","contrary_evidence":["The administration said the measure was meant to address insecurity and protect civilians."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.4","4B.8","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"National convention’s decisions could herald new era for journalists in DRC","publisher":"Reporters Without Borders","publication_date":"2022-02-22","url":"https://rsf.org/en/national-convention-s-decisions-could-herald-new-era-journalists-drc","claim":"RSF says Tshisekedi presided over a January 2022 media convention, reiterated his desire to guarantee journalist safety through a dedicated alert mechanism, and the convention recommended abolishing prison sentences for press offences and imposing a moratorium on arrests of journalists.","locator":"lines 325-328","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct RSF report with clear date, named presidential role, and specific reform proposals for the press environment.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year and aimed at reforms implemented during 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Tshisekedi, who presided over the convention and publicly endorsed the reforms.","contrary_evidence":["RSF frames the reforms as proposals and encouragement, not proof of implemented legal change during 2022."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.6","4B.5"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Two DRC radio stations suspended, transmitters seized over broadcasts criticizing politicians","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-11-28","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/11/two-drc-radio-stations-suspended-transmitters-seized-over-broadcasts-criticizing-politicians/","claim":"CPJ reports that on October 25, 2022, Sankuru administrator Bono Emakitshi suspended Radio Losanganya and Radio Grand Tam-tam and ordered their transmitters seized over broadcasts critical of politicians.","locator":"lines 516-519","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Named officials, dated directive, specific outlets, and a clear press-freedom restriction documented by CPJ.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to ruler responsibility because it reflects state-level censorship under Tshisekedi's administration.","contrary_evidence":["The immediate action came from a provincial administrator, not a presidential decree."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"DRC journalist Olivier Makambu jailed over broadcast following defamation complaint","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-11-23","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/11/drc-journalist-olivier-makambu-jailed-over-broadcast-following-defamation-complaint/","claim":"CPJ says police arrested journalist Olivier Makambu after a defamation complaint over a broadcast about interference in a local succession dispute, and CPJ warned that repeated arrests show the press is not safe under Felix Tshisekedi's presidency.","locator":"lines 516-519","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific case report with arrest date, legal basis, and explicit press-freedom assessment from CPJ.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to state treatment of journalists under Tshisekedi's presidency, even though the complaint originated locally.","contrary_evidence":["The arrest followed a formal complaint and warrant process, so the abuse is legal harassment rather than purely extrajudicial detention."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"French journalist Sonia Rolley expelled from DRC, denied accreditation","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-11-09","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/11/french-journalist-sonia-rolley-expelled-from-drc-denied-accreditation/","claim":"CPJ says DRC immigration authorities summoned and expelled Reuters journalist Sonia Rolley after her accreditation was not approved, and CPJ described it as further evidence of deteriorating press freedom.","locator":"lines 516-524","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Clear named case with direct attribution to a state agency and corroboration from Reuters and RFI cited in the article.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly relevant to the Tshisekedi administration because the expulsion was carried out by a national immigration authority overseeing press access.","contrary_evidence":["The government described the decision as administrative rather than a press-freedom action."],"lenses":["4B.6","4B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congo’s Indigenous Rights Bill Stalls","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-10-28","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/10/28/congos-indigenous-rights-bill-stalls","claim":"HRW notes that on November 16, 2022, President Felix Tshisekedi signed the new law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Indigenous Pygmy Peoples, after the bill had awaited his signature.","locator":"lines 615-618","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct HRW update with a precise signature date and a rights-expansion law aimed at an excluded group.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributed to Tshisekedi's personal signature of the law.","contrary_evidence":["The article also notes the bill had stalled for months before the signature, so the positive step was delayed."],"lenses":["4B.7","4B.10","4B.4"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Compte rendu de la soixante-deuxième réunion du Conseil des Ministres","publisher":"Présidence de la République Démocratique du Congo","publication_date":"2022-07-15","url":"https://presidence.cd/conseil-de-ministres/compte_rendu_de_la_soixante_deuxieme_reunion_du_conseil_des_ministres","claim":"The presidential council report says Tshisekedi praised the promulgation of the law on persons living with disabilities, called it the first such framework in the DRC, and ordered the government to finalize implementing regulations so the protection would be effective.","locator":"lines 91-100","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary presidential record of the meeting, with direct statements by Tshisekedi and concrete implementation instructions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Tshisekedi as head of state and source of the instruction.","contrary_evidence":["The text shows a promise and implementation directive, not proof that the law was already fully effective in 2022."],"lenses":["4B.4","4B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Congo schedules presidential elections for Dec 2023","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-27","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/27/congo-politics","claim":"Reuters reported that Congo said it would hold presidential and parliamentary elections on December 20, 2023, that the government pledged to stick to the timetable, and that the spokesman said there was no question of negotiating constitutional deadlines; the report also notes presidents are limited to two terms under Congolese law.","locator":"lines 666-678","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters wire story carried by Euronews with a precise date, direct quotations, and explicit term-limit framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 evidence about 2023 electoral planning and constitutional timing within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to the government under Tshisekedi, through the spokesman's public commitment to respect deadlines.","contrary_evidence":["This is a pledge about future elections rather than proof of completed clean transfers or non-interference in practice."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"RDC : La CENI publie le calendrier électoral du cycle 2022-2027","publisher":"Radio Okapi","publication_date":"2022-11-26","url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/2022/11/26/actualite/politique/rdc-la-ceni-publie-le-calendrier-electoral-du-cycle-2022-2027","claim":"Radio Okapi reports that CENI published the 2022-2027 electoral calendar, with voter registration starting on December 24, 2022, the presidential election set for December 20, 2023, and CENI saying delay was not in its vocabulary.","locator":"lines 150-161","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct local reporting on the election body's public announcement with precise dates and a clear quotation about delay.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year and the opening of the next electoral cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but important: it reflects the electoral timetable under Tshisekedi's administration and the election body's public posture.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports CENI's statement, so it does not itself verify later implementation."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Several journalists detained, prosecuted - Civicus Monitor","publisher":"Civicus Monitor","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://monitor.civicus.org/explore/several-journalists-detained-prosecuted/","claim":"Civicus says JED documented at least 124 press freedom violations in 2022 in the DRC, including 37 arrests, 18 physical assaults, 17 bans on radio stations or programmes, 2 abductions, and 1 killing, and it quotes JED describing press freedom under Tshisekedi as fragile and worsening.","locator":"lines 59-66","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Secondary rights-monitor summary of a national watchdog report with concrete counts and a direct quotation, though it is not the original report itself.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year.","ruler_attribution":"Broadly relevant to the Tshisekedi administration because the report describes the national press environment during his tenure.","contrary_evidence":["The figures mix state, local, and non-state abuses, so not every incident is directly presidentially ordered."],"lenses":["4B.3","4B.6","4B.9"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found this wave: about 22.
- Documents opened this wave: 17.
- Duplicate families rejected: 6.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items rejected: 3.
- Inaccessible items: 4.
- Accepted distinct URLs this wave: 10.
- Accepted distinct URLs cumulative across both waves: 30.
- Distinct domains cumulative across both waves: at least 14.

Material gaps and next best directions:
- Direct 2022 evidence on election-rule manipulation and CENI capture by Tshisekedi himself is still thinner than the repression and media record.
- Direct 2022 evidence on surveillance, digital controls, and internet shutdowns remains sparse.
- Direct evidence on term-limit pressure and succession maneuvering would be stronger if tied to constitutional texts, court rulings, or elite bargaining rather than only public pledges.
- Political-equality evidence beyond indigenous rights and disability inclusion is still thin for women, opposition regions, and unpopular viewpoints.

Next best query/source directions:
